IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg8-nouns`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 263 (piece dg8, lines 1277 to 1300):
-- merger or consolidation of domestic corporations and partnerships; service of process upon the surviving or resulting
-- corporation or partnership.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online, made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- Quote lines below are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N, and an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation. This module states the law as a relation
-- between the corporation, its stockholders, the partnerships and the Secretary of State; the seat layer dg8-seat.l4 asks it
-- from the person's side.
--
-- What the section leaves to law outside this module is an input (named for the fact, with its section), and is listed in NOTES.md:
--   * how a corporation adopts, approves and files a merger agreement, and when it takes effect: sections 251 and 255 (pieces dg6, dg7);
--   * how a certificate is executed: section 103 (piece dg1); fractional shares: section 155 (piece dg3);
--   * the fee for service on the Secretary of State: section 391(a)(29) (piece dg11);
--   * the law of the jurisdiction under which a partnership is formed (prohibition of the merger, approval by the partnership,
--     provisions it requires in the agreement): not among the inputs.
-- Section 114(a) reads "stockholder" as "member" for a nonstock corporation; subsection (b) of section 114 does not take section 263 out of that
-- reading (only section 267 is out, in this piece), so "stockholder" here includes a member of a nonstock corporation.

§ `s 263(a) Corporations of this State and partnerships may merge or consolidate`

-- "Partnership" is defined for this section only: a general partnership (including a limited liability partnership) or a limited
-- partnership (including a limited liability limited partnership), formed under the laws of this State or of any other jurisdiction.
-- src:1278 | The term “partnership” as used in this section includes any partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)) formed under the laws of this State or the laws of any other jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(a) (src:1278)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(a) the term partnership` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a general partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The power: 1 or more corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with 1 or more partnerships,
-- unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which the partnership or partnerships are formed prohibit it.
-- The four forms the combination may take (merger into a surviving corporation or partnership; consolidation into a new
-- resulting corporation of this State or a new partnership) are the constructors of the form in dg8-nouns.
-- src:1278 | (a) Any 1 or more corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with 1 or more partnerships (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such partnership or partnerships are formed prohibit such merger or consolidation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(a) (src:1278)
GIVEN `the number of corporations of this State that are to merge or consolidate` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of partnerships that are to merge or consolidate` IS A NUMBER
      `the laws of a jurisdiction under which a partnership is formed prohibit the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(a) corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with partnerships` MEANS
        `the number of corporations of this State that are to merge or consolidate` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the number of partnerships that are to merge or consolidate` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `the laws of a jurisdiction under which a partnership is formed prohibit the merger or consolidation`)

§ `s 263(b) The agreement of merger or consolidation`

-- src:1279 | (b) Each such corporation and partnership shall enter into a written agreement of merger or consolidation. The agreement shall state:
-- src:1280 | (1) The terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation;
-- src:1281 | (2) The mode of carrying the same into effect;
-- src:1282 | (3) In the case of a merger in which the surviving entity is a corporation of this State, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation;
-- src:1283 | (4) In the case of a consolidation in which the resulting entity is a corporation of this State, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement;
-- src:1284 | (5) The manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock of each such corporation and the partnership interests of each such partnership into shares, partnership interests or other securities of the entity surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation or of cancelling some or all of such shares or interests, …
-- src:1284 | and if any shares of any such corporation or any partnership interests of any such partnership are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into shares, partnership interests or other securities of the entity surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of such shares or partnership interests are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of such shares or partnership interests and the surrender of any certificates evidencing them, …
-- src:1286 | (7) Such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation (including any provision for amendment of the partnership agreement and statement of partnership existence or certificate of limited partnership (or equivalent documents) of the surviving partnership) by the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the partnerships are formed.
-- The agreement is a written agreement entered into by each corporation and partnership and it states (1) to (5) and (7). The
-- statements are facts about the document: one BOOLEAN per limb. Limb (6), "such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable",
-- is read as permissive and is the rule further down (fork F4).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b) (src:1279-1286)
DECLARE `s 263(b) Statements in the agreement of merger or consolidation` HAS
    `s 263(b)(1) the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 263(b)(2) the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 263(b)(3) the agreement states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 263(b)(4) the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 263(b)(5) the agreement states the manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock and the partnership interests into securities of the surviving or resulting entity, or of cancelling some or all of them`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 263(b)(5) the agreement states the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity that the holders of shares or interests not to remain outstanding are to receive`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 263(b)(7) the agreement sets out the other provisions or facts that the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the partnerships are formed require`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b) (src:1279-1286)
GIVEN `each corporation and partnership has entered into a written agreement of merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `dg8 Form of a combination`
      `some shares or partnership interests are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into securities of the surviving or resulting entity or to be cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holders of those shares or interests are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      statements IS A `s 263(b) Statements in the agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(b) the agreement of merger or consolidation is as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `each corporation and partnership has entered into a written agreement of merger or consolidation`
    AND statements's `s 263(b)(1) the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`
    AND statements's `s 263(b)(2) the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`
    -- (3) only "in the case of a merger in which the surviving entity is a corporation of this State"
    AND (   (NOT (`dg8 the combination is a merger into a surviving corporation` form))
         OR statements's `s 263(b)(3) the agreement states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation`)
    -- (4) only "in the case of a consolidation in which the resulting entity is a corporation of this State"
    AND (   (NOT (`dg8 the combination is a consolidation into a resulting corporation` form))
         OR statements's `s 263(b)(4) the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement`)
    AND statements's `s 263(b)(5) the agreement states the manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock and the partnership interests into securities of the surviving or resulting entity, or of cancelling some or all of them`
    -- (5), second limb: "if any shares ... are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into ... or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders ... are to receive" (fork F3)
    AND (   (NOT (`some shares or partnership interests are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into securities of the surviving or resulting entity or to be cancelled` AND `the holders of those shares or interests are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity`))
         OR statements's `s 263(b)(5) the agreement states the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity that the holders of shares or interests not to remain outstanding are to receive`)
    AND statements's `s 263(b)(7) the agreement sets out the other provisions or facts that the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the partnerships are formed require`

-- (6): "Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including ... a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance
-- or recognition of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests ... or for some other arrangement with respect thereto,
-- consistent with § 155". Read as permissive: a detail the constituents deem desirable may be included; an arrangement for fractions
-- must be consistent with section 155 (piece dg3, taken as an input).
-- src:1285 | (6) Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership or of any other corporation or entity the shares, rights, other securities or interests of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for some other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b)(6) (src:1285)
GIVEN `the constituents deem the detail or provision desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests, or some other arrangement for them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement is consistent with § 155` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 155 (piece dg3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(b)(6) the detail or provision may be included in the agreement` MEANS
        `the constituents deem the detail or provision desirable`
    AND (   (NOT `it is a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests, or some other arrangement for them`)
         OR `the arrangement is consistent with § 155`)

-- A term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement, provided that the manner in which the facts operate on the term
-- is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement. (The next sentence, which says what "facts" includes, is inert: keel instruction 15.)
-- src:1287 | Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b) (src:1287)
GIVEN `the term depends on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which those facts operate on the term is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(b) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` MEANS
        (NOT `the term depends on facts ascertainable outside the agreement`)
    OR  `the manner in which those facts operate on the term is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement`

-- The sentence after it: "The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation."
-- "Includes, but is not limited to" makes the list of facts open; it does not make everything a fact. An event, and a determination or action by any person or body
-- (including the corporation), are facts; for anything else the text does not say, so the rule answers NOTHING (fork F26).
-- src:1287 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b) (src:1287)
DECLARE `s 263(b) Kind of fact` IS ONE OF
    `the occurrence of an event under s 263(b)`
    `a determination by any person or body, including the corporation, under s 263(b)`
    `an action by any person or body, including the corporation, under s 263(b)`
    `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 263(b)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b) (src:1287)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 263(b) Kind of fact`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263(b) the kind of fact is within the term facts` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 263(b)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 263(c) Approval, filing and effect; the certificate of merger or consolidation`

-- The agreement is adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by each corporation in the same manner as in section 251
-- or 255 (pieces dg6 and dg7, an input), and by each partnership in accordance with its partnership agreement and the laws of the
-- jurisdiction under which it is formed (outside the inputs, an input). If the surviving or resulting entity is a partnership, each
-- stockholder of a merging corporation who will become a general partner of it must also approve.
-- src:1288 | The agreement required by subsection (b) of this section shall be adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the corporations in the same manner as is provided in § 251 or § 255 of this title and, in the case of the partnerships, in accordance with their partnership agreements and in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction under which they are formed. …
-- src:1288 | If the surviving or resulting entity is a partnership, in addition to any other approvals, each stockholder of a merging corporation who will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership must approve the agreement of merger or consolidation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c) (src:1288)
DECLARE `s 263(c) Approvals of the agreement` HAS
    `s 263(c) each corporation has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in the same manner as is provided in § 251 or § 255`  IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: sections 251, 255 (pieces dg6, dg7)
    `s 263(c) each partnership has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in accordance with its partnership agreement and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed`  IS A BOOLEAN -- law outside the inputs
    `s 263(c) a stockholder of a merging corporation will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 263(c) each stockholder who will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership has approved the agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c) (src:1288)
GIVEN form IS A `dg8 Form of a combination`
      approvals IS A `s 263(c) Approvals of the agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(c) the agreement has the approvals the subsection requires` MEANS
        approvals's `s 263(c) each corporation has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in the same manner as is provided in § 251 or § 255`
    AND approvals's `s 263(c) each partnership has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in accordance with its partnership agreement and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed`
    -- "in addition to any other approvals": only where the surviving or resulting entity is a partnership
    AND (   (NOT (`dg8 the combination ends in an entity that is not a corporation` form
                  AND approvals's `s 263(c) a stockholder of a merging corporation will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership`))
         OR approvals's `s 263(c) each stockholder who will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership has approved the agreement`)

-- The stockholder's side of the same relation: a stockholder who will become a general partner of a surviving or resulting partnership
-- must approve, so the merger cannot make that stockholder a general partner without that stockholder's approval.
-- src:1288 | If the surviving or resulting entity is a partnership, in addition to any other approvals, each stockholder of a merging corporation who will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership must approve the agreement of merger or consolidation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c) (src:1288)
GIVEN form IS A `dg8 Form of a combination`
      `the stockholder will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(c) the stockholder must approve the agreement` MEANS
        `dg8 the combination ends in an entity that is not a corporation` form
    AND `the stockholder will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership`

-- The agreement is filed and becomes effective for all purposes of the laws of this State when and as section 251 or 255 provides
-- for the merger or consolidation of corporations of this State (pieces dg6, dg7: the date is an input). A certificate filed in lieu
-- of the agreement (below) stands for it.
-- src:1288 | The agreement shall be filed and shall become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State when and as provided in § 251 or § 255 of this title with respect to the merger or consolidation of corporations of this State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c) (src:1288)
GIVEN `the agreement, or a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in lieu of it, has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the merger or consolidation becomes effective as provided in § 251 or § 255` IS A DATE -- out of range: sections 251, 255 (pieces dg6, dg7)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(c) the merger or consolidation is effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` MEANS
        `the agreement, or a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in lieu of it, has been filed`
    AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `the date on which the merger or consolidation becomes effective as provided in § 251 or § 255`

-- The certificate that may be filed in lieu of the agreement states (1) to (8). (4) is for a merger in which a corporation is the
-- surviving entity; (5) for a consolidation in which a corporation is the resulting entity; (8) is "the agreement, if any, required
-- by subsection (d)", which is required only of a surviving or resulting partnership formed under the laws of another jurisdiction.
-- src:1288 | In lieu of filing the agreement of merger or consolidation, the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership may file a certificate of merger or consolidation, executed in accordance with § 103 of this title, if the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation, or by a general partner, if the surviving or resulting entity is a partnership, which states:
-- src:1289 | (1) The name, jurisdiction of formation or organization and type of entity of each of the constituent entities;
-- src:1290 | (2) That an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent entities in accordance with this subsection;
-- src:1291 | (3) The name of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership;
-- src:1292 | (4) In the case of a merger in which a corporation is the surviving entity, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation;
-- src:1293 | (5) In the case of a consolidation in which a corporation is the resulting entity, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the certificate;
-- src:1294 | (6) That the executed agreement of consolidation or merger is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership and the address thereof;
-- src:1295 | (7) That a copy of the agreement of consolidation or merger will be furnished by the surviving or resulting entity, on request and without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation or any partner of any constituent partnership; and
-- src:1296 | (8) The agreement, if any, required by subsection (d) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c) (src:1288-1296)
