§ `s 263(d) Service of process on the surviving or resulting partnership`

-- If the entity surviving or resulting is a partnership formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State, it shall agree
-- (a) that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding to enforce an obligation of any constituent corporation or
-- partnership of this State or an obligation of the survivor arising from the merger or consolidation, including a suit to enforce
-- the right of stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings under section 262, (b) irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as
-- its agent to accept service, and (c) specify the address to which the Secretary of State is to mail a copy of the process.
-- src:1297 | If the entity surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation is a partnership formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State, it shall agree that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation or partnership of this State, as well as for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership arising from the merger or consolidation, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to § 262 of this title, and shall irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings and shall specify the address to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d) (src:1297)
GIVEN form IS A `dg8 Form of a combination`
      `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 263(d) the surviving or resulting partnership must agree to be served with process in this State` MEANS
        `dg8 the combination ends in an entity that is not a corporation` form
    AND `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`

-- What the surviving or resulting partnership has to say in its agreement (four statements).
